  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MYOMY do goods and Leatherina: Fair trade and sustainable hand crafted leather bags from Dhaka, Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MYOMY do goods designs and sells sustainable and fair trade leather bags and is one of few companies in the fashion industry that is a member of the WFTO. Because of high demand, the need to spread risks and reaching the maximum capacity of its main partner in India, the company was looking for a second production partner. This search led to Bangladesh due to its role as a fashion manufacturer as well as recent misconducts and accidents in the industry which MYOMY do goods aims to address through its business model. After explorative meetings with Leatherina, Technical Assistance (DGGF-TA) provided support to test and improve production capacity of Leatherina, find adequate tanneries that comply with worldwide sustainability standards, assess feasibility of a joint venture and offer guidance and advise to meet international standards to produce for and export to the European market. Part of the project was the set-up of a quality control system to asses and minimise risks of parties involved and address social and environmental issues. The project directly supported 31 jobs and indirectly supported over 200 jobs. Knowledge transfer was ensured by training 31 people on the sustainable production of bags which contributes to improved working conditions and production processes for people involved as well as higher production capacity. Further expansion plans are currently being explored and may lead to additional jobs being supported in Bangladesh.</narrative>
  </description>
